is\n    25\t   `{:phase :put|:verify-unissued|:verify-issued :address a :put-id n\n    26\t   :get-id m?}` — an address, never a payload: nothing this layer retains\n    27\t   or publishes carries a payload (the N11 discipline the blocking driver\n    28\t   owes, held here by construction).  `:routes` maps every wire id a\n    29\t   record currently claims — its put id while `:put`, its verify get id\n    30\t   while `:verify-issued` — to the record's put id, which is the identity\n    31\t   a materialization's one published completion carries.\n    32\t\n    33\t   `step` advances in one fixed order, and the order is load-bearing:\n    34\t\n    35\t   1. re-attempt the retained `:unsent` envelope through `rpc/request!`\n    36\t      (which retries it and ignores the operation it is given), folding\n    37\t      the outcome under `:attempt`;\n    38\t   2. `rpc/poll!` at most `budget` response-medium elements;\n    39\t   3. if the state is terminal and an `:unsent` envelope remains, abandon\n    40\t      it with the terminal reason, so its loss surfaces on the ordinary\n   245\t         reg (or (get jing/registry algo)\n   246\t                 (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\n   247\t                                 {:algorithm algo})))\n   248\t         addr (keyword \"segment\"\n   249\t                       (str (:address-id reg) \"-\" (jing/digest-bytes algo bs)))]\n   250\t     (submit state put-content-op [addr (jing/bytes->base64 bs)] true))))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn- accepted-bytes\n   254\t  \"The canonical bytes a `:jing/get-content` envelope carries for address\n   255\t   as Base64 text, or nil when the text is not strict Base64 or the bytes\n   256\t   do not hash to the address.\"\n   257\t  [address b64]\n   258\t  (try (let [bs (jing/base64->bytes b64)]\n   259\t         (when (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs) bs))\n   260\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   261\t