(fn [_address & _]\n   334\t                                           @malformed-response)}\n   335\t        client (remote/content-client ::mock\n   336\t                                      (fn [_ op args]\n   337\t                                        (apply (get mock-handlers op) args))\n   338\t                                      (fn [_] nil))\n   339\t        addr (jing/segment-key {:x 1})]\n   340\t    (try (doseq [val [\"bogus\" {:found? \"yes\", :value nil} {:found? true}\n   341\t                      {:value 123} {:found? true, :value 123, :extra 4}\n   342\t                      {:found? true, :value 123}\n   343\t                      {:found? true, :value \"not base64!\"}]]\n   344\t           (reset! malformed-response val)\n   345\t           (try (jing/get client addr ::miss)\n   346\t                (is false\n   347\t                    (str \"should have thrown for malformed response: \"\n   348\t                         (pr-str val)))\n   349\t                (catch #?(:clj Exception\n   350\t                          :cljs js/Error\n   351\t                          :cljd Object)\n   352\t                       e\n   353\t                  (let [data (ex-data e)\n   354\t                        msg #?(:clj (.getMessage e)\n   355\t                               :cljs (.-message e)\n   356\t                               :cljd (ex-message e))]\n   357\t                    (is (= :jing/get-content (:operation data)))\n   358\t                    (is (= addr (:address data)))\n   359\t                    (is (= val (:response data)))\n   360\t                    (is (re-find #\"malformed RPC response\" msg))))))\n   361\t         (finally (jing/close! client)))))\n   362\t\n   363\t\n   364\t(deftest local-present-then-absent-test\n   365\t  (let [mock-handlers {:jing/put-content (fn [_address _payload & _] :present),\n   366\t                       :jing/get-content (fn [_address & _]\n   367\t                                           {:found? false, :value nil})}\n   368\t        client (remote/content-client ::mock\n   369\t                                      (fn [_ op args]\n   370\t                                        (apply (get mock-handlers op) args))\n   371\t                                      (fn [_] nil))]\n   372\t    (try\n   373\t      ;; nil case\n   374\t      (is (thrown-with-msg?\n   375\t            #?(:clj Exception\n   376\t               :cljs js/Error\n   377\t               :cljd Object)\n   378\t            #\"backend reported :present but the content address is absent\"\n   379\t            (jing/materialize! client nil)))\n   380\t      ;; non-nil case\n   381\t      (is (thrown-with-msg?\n   382\t            #?(:clj Exception\n   383\t               :cljs js/Error\n   384\t               :cljd Object)\n   385\t            #\"backend reported :present but the content address is absent\"\n   386\t            (jing/materialize! client {:some \"payload\"})))\n   387\t      (finally (jing/close! client)))))\n   388\t\n   389\t\n   390\t(deftest network-presence-envelope-test\n   116\t- Encode once before a write, derive the address from those bytes, and pass\n   117\t  those same bytes to the backend. On `:present`, read back and verify the\n   118\t  bytes by hash and byte-for-byte equality with the proposed payload. Never\n   119\t  overwrite conflicting content. Return an address only after\n   120\t  the backend reports its applicable storage guarantee.\n   121\t- The wrapper derives and verifies addresses; a backend re-verifies a put\n   122\t  exactly when bytes arrive from an untrusted party, such as a remote/DHT\n   123\t  server checking a client's claim.\n   124\t- Verify every retrieved payload against its requested address before\n   125\t  decoding exactly one supported value. Canonicality verification (decode,\n   126\t  re-encode, byte-compare) occurs exactly once at each ingress of bytes Jing\n   127\t  did not encode itself: remote/DHT receipt and file replay acceptance,\n   128\t  before storage, caching, or exposure. Ordinary reads of accepted snapshots\n   129\t  hash-verify and decode without re-encoding. Validation belongs to the\n   130\t  shared codec/wrapper at those boundaries, not to backend value handlers;\n   131\t  immutable local forwarding does not repeat ingress validation. Missing\n   132\t  content remains distinct from stored nil, which has a CBOR representation.\n   445\tand re-encoded value. Duplicate digests require identical payload bytes.\n   446\tPostgreSQL byte columns and S3 objects obey the same ingress rule when opened\n   447\tover externally supplied bytes.\n   448\t\n   449\t### Remote and DHT\n   450\t\n   451\tCarry canonical payload bytes as padded standard-alphabet Base64 strings\n   452\t(no whitespace or URL-safe alphabet) inside the existing Transit\n   453\toperation envelopes. Encode and decode this transport representation at\n   454\tJing's network boundaries; leave general DaoStream Transit unchanged.\n   455\tRemote and DHT APIs above the byte-store wrapper remain value-facing.\n   456\t\n   457\tDecode Base64 strictly, hash-verify received bytes against the claimed\n   458\taddress, and perform the one ingress canonicality check before accepting or\n   459\tcaching them. Preserve explicit presence indicators, idempotent writes,\n   460\tcorrelated remote errors, and DHT refusal/next-candidate behavior. A found\n   461\tnil travels as Base64 of CBOR nil; an absent envelope keeps its explicit\n   462\tfalse indicator and nil placeholder, which is not Base64-decoded.\n   463\t\n   464\tThe only current Jing application-level message byte cap is the DHT UDP\n   545\t  \"Retrieve the value stored at a content address.\n   546\t\n   547\t   Only valid registered content addresses are valid DaoJing reads;\n   548\t   arbitrary keys and mutable roots are outside DaoJing and throw before the\n   549\t   backend is consulted. The backend's bytes are hash-verified against the\n   550\t   address and decoded; bytes that do not hash to the address throw.\n   551\t   Returns not-found when the address is absent.\"\n   552\t  [handle address not-found]\n   553\t  (when-not (segment-address? address)\n   554\t    (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing reads only valid segment content addresses\"\n   555\t                    {:address address})))\n   556\t  (let [get-fn (:get-bytes-fn handle)]\n   557\t    (when-not (fn? get-fn)\n   558\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :get-bytes-fn\"\n   559\t                      {:handle handle})))\n   560\t    (let [stored (get-fn address not-found)]\n   561\t      (if (identical? stored not-found)\n   562\t        not-found\n   563\t        (segment-value address stored)))))\n   564\t\n   565\t\n   566\t(defn close!\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I found another remote receipt path outside the stepped client: the blocking `content-client` turns a found Base64 reply into bytes and returns them to `jing/get`, whose trusted-snapshot decoder no longer checks canonicality. I’m checking its response contract and test coverage now; this appears to leave the same hash-valid, noncanonical payload exposure that the new stepped-client test closes."}}
