ing. Strip `:line`, `:column`, `:end-line`, and `:end-column`; omit empty\n   181\t  metadata. Clear metadata on internally constructed Dart collections\n   182\t  before attaching supplied metadata. Do not strip arbitrary user `:tag`\n   183\t  metadata as a workaround for Dart constructor metadata. This clearing\n   184\t  covers only collections Jing constructs at decode: a Dart producer\n   185\t  building a payload with `list` must still clear ClojureDart's constructor\n   186\t  metadata itself (`(with-meta (apply list xs) nil)`); that `dao.jing.md`\n   187\t  open item carries forward, it is not retired by this plan.\n   188\t- Encode **all** keywords and symbols as tag 27 with `dao.jing/keyword` or\n   450\t\n   451\tCarry canonical payload bytes as padded standard-alphabet Base64 strings\n   452\t(no whitespace or URL-safe alphabet) inside the existing Transit\n   453\toperation envelopes. Encode and decode this transport representation at\n   454\tJing's network boundaries; leave general DaoStream Transit unchanged.\n   455\tRemote and DHT APIs above the byte-store wrapper remain value-facing.\n   456\t\n   457\tDecode Base64 strictly, hash-verify received bytes against the claimed\n   458\taddress, and perform the one ingress canonicality check before accepting or\n   459\tcaching them. Preserve explicit presence indicators, idempotent writes,\n   460\tcorrelated remote errors, and DHT refusal/next-candidate behavior. A found\n   461\tnil travels as Base64 of CBOR nil; an absent envelope keeps its explicit\n   462\tfalse indicator and nil placeholder, which is not Base64-decoded.\n   634\t  unifying against each other in a query.\n   635\t- Malformed and noncanonical encodings; duplicate keys; unknown tags;\n   636\t  duplicate set elements and decoded equality collapse; TaggedValue and\n   637\t  unsupported SimpleValue; native CBOR floats; invalid UTF-8; trailing data;\n   638\t  unsupported host values; address mismatches. Hash-valid noncanonical\n   639\t  payloads fail at ingress; repeated local hydration hash-verifies every\n   640\t  time without repeating canonical re-encoding.\n   641\t- File reopen, duplicate insertion, durability failures, torn tails,\n   642\t  complete corrupt frames, raw digest length/mismatch, and nondestructive\n   895\t\n   896\t\n   897\t(defn encode-value\n   898\t  \"Encode one canonical-domain value under its value-table class: the\n   899\t   full tagged, length-delimited part, under the settled D3 byte rules —\n   900\t   int64 little-endian two's complement for integers, IEEE-754 bits with\n   901\t   one quiet-NaN encoding for doubles (1 and 1.0 stay distinct), UTF-8 byte\n   902\t   lengths, NFC strings and ident parts. Maps and sets sort by their encoded\n   903\t   parts, the Section 5 order rule; vectors and lists are the distinct classes\n   904\t   the D0 ruling split. An out-of-domain value is a diagnostic.\"\n   905\t  [v]\n   906\t  (let [class (canonical-class v)]\n   907\t    (case class\n   908\t      :nil (framed :nil \"\")\n   909\t      :bool (framed :bool (if v \"01\" \"00\"))\n   910\t      :int64 (framed :int64 (int64-le-hex v))\n   911\t      :double (framed :double (double-le-hex v))\n   912\t      :string (framed :string (normalize-nfc v))\n   913\t      :bytes (framed :bytes (apply str (map #(to-hex (bit-and % 0xff) 2) v)))\n   914\t      :keyword (framed :keyword (ident-content v))\n   915\t      :symbol (framed :symbol (ident-content v))\n   916\t      :map (let [entries (sort (map (fn [[k x]]\n   917\t                                      [(encode-value k) (encode-value x)])\n   918\t                                    v))]\n   919\t             (when (some (fn [[a b]] (= (first a) (first b)))\n   920\t                         (partition 2 1 entries))\n   921\t               (throw (ex-info \"Map keys collide in canonical encoding\"\n   922\t                               {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v})))\n   923\t             (framed :map (app