{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-24 19:23:41 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 02:23:41 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**R2 finding 3: PARTIALLY CLOSED.** The stepped client now strictly decodes a hash-verified receipt and maps refusal to `integrity-failure` ([step.cljc:316](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/remote/step.cljc:316)). Its single opaque-object sentinel avoids both keyword identity differences and collision with a decoded value ([step.cljc:269](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/remote/step.cljc:269)). The new test uses an address hashed over noncanonical `18 01` bytes, so it exercises canonicality independently of the digest check ([step_test.cljc:275](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/jing/remote/step_test.cljc:275)).\n\nP1 | [remote.cljc:136](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/remote.cljc:136) | The blocking `content-client` returns a found reply after Base64 decoding alone ([remote.cljc:139](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/remote.cljc:139)). `jing/get` then uses `segment-value`, which hash-verifies but calls `decode-snapshot` rather than checking canonicality ([jing.cljc:457](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:457)). A hostile server can therefore serve hash-valid, noncanonical bytes under their own address and expose the decoded value, contrary to the remote-ingress contract ([dao.jing.cbor.md:124](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:124)). | Hash-verify and call strict `cbor/decode` on each found blocking-client receipt before returning its bytes; add the same hostile-pair test to `remote_test.cljc`.\n\nThe Dart list fix clears constructor metadata only on the newly built projected list ([debruijn.cljc:1006](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1006)); it does not discard arbitrary `:tag` metadata in the codec, and the Merkle value encoder does not use metadata ([debruijn.cljc:897](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:897), [dao.jing.cbor.md:179](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:179)). The quoted Dart fixtures address the constructor-metadata failure ([jing_test.cljc:225](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/jing_test.cljc:225), [vm_test.cljc:625](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm_test.cljc:625)). I did not rerun the suites; the orchestrator records all three lanes green ([orchestrator-log.md:6941](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/orchestrator-log.md:6941)).\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES"}}
